INSERT INTO `{tbl_prefix}pages_translations` (`page_id`, `language_id`, `page_title`, `page_content`) VALUES
(1, @language_id, 'About us', '<div style=\"margin: auto; width: 98%;\"><font style=\"font-weight: bold;\" size=\"4\">About Us</font><hr noshade=\"noshade\" size=\"1\">\r\n  \r\n  \r\n    <p><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">ClipBucketV5 </span>is one of the world\'s best video sites . We specialize in short-form\r\noriginal content - from new, emerging talents and established Hollywood\r\nheavyweights alike. We\'re committed to delivering an exceptional\r\nentertainment experience, and we do so by engaging and empowering our\r\naudience every step of the way.</p>\r\n      <p>Everyone can Watch Videos\r\non <span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">ClipBucketV5</span>. People can see first-hand accounts of current events, find\r\nvideos about their hobbies and interests, and discover the\r\nquirky and unusual. As more people capture special moments on\r\nvideo,<span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">ClipBucketV5 </span>is empowering them to become the broadcasters of\r\ntomorrow.</p>\r\n      <p><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">ClipBucketV5 </span>not only a video sharing website but\r\nalso has social network features, you can make friends,\r\nand send them videos and private messages. <span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">ClipBucketV5 </span><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\"></span> also has built in\r\nrating system and comment system so that people can discuss on there\r\ninterested videos, not only comment but also, people can rate Comments.</p></div>'),
(2, @language_id, 'Privacy Policy', '<h1>ClipBucketV5 Privacy Notice\r\n</h1>\r\n<h2>Personal Information</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n  <li><strong>Browsing ClipBucketV5</strong> By default, you can watch videos on ClipBucketV5 without having a ClipBucketV5 Account. You also can contact us through the <a href="https://clipbucket.oxygenz.fr" target="_blank">ClipBucketV5 contact form</a> or by creating a <a href="https://github.com/MacWarrior/clipbucket-v5/issues" target="_blank">GitHub issue</a>.</li>\r\n <li><strong>Your ClipBucketV5 Account.</strong> For some activities on ClipBucketV5, like uploading videos, posting  comments, flagging videos, or watching restricted videos, you need a ClipBucketV5. We ask for some personal information when you create an account, including your email address and a password, which is used to protect your account from unauthorized access.</li>\r\n <li><strong>Usage Information.</strong> When you use ClipBucketV5, we may record information about your usage of the site, such as the channels and favorites you subscribe to, which other users you communicate with, the videos you watch, the frequency and size of data transfers, and information you display about yourself as well as information you click on in ClipBucketV5 (including UI elements, settings). If you are logged in, we may associate that information with your ClipBucketV5 Account. In order to ensure the quality of our service to you, we may place a tag (also called a \"web beacon\") in HTML-based customer support emails or other communications with you in order to confirm delivery.</li>\r\n <li><strong>Content Uploaded to Site.</strong> Any personal information or video content that you voluntarily disclose online (e.g., video comments, your profile page) may be collected and used by others. If you download the ClipBucketV5 Uploader, your copy includes a unique application number. This number, and information  about your installation of the Uploader (version number, language) will be sent to ClipBucketV5 when the Uploader automatically checks for updates and will be used to update your version of the Uploader.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>Uses</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n  <li>If you submit personal information to ClipBucketV5, we may use that information to operate, maintain, and improve the features and functionality of ClipBucketV5, and to process any flagging activity or other communication you send to us.</li>\r\n <li>We do not use your email address or other personal information to send commercial or marketing messages without your consent. We may use your email address without further consent for non-marketing or administrative purposes (such as notifying you of major ClipBucketV5 changes or for customer service  purposes). You also can choose how often ClipBucketV5 sends you email updates in your ClipBucketV5 Account settings page.</li>\r\n <li>We use cookies, web beacons, and log file information to: (a) store information so that you will not have to re-enter it during your visit or the next time you visit ClipBucketV5; (b) provide custom, personalized content and information; (c) monitor the effectiveness of our marketing campaigns; (d) monitor aggregate metrics such as total number of visitors and pages viewed; and (e) track your entries, submissions, and status in promotions, sweepstakes, and contests.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>Information That is Publicly Available</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>When you create a ClipBucketV5 Account, some information about your ClipBucketV5 Account and your account activity will be provided to other users of ClipBucketV5. This may include the date you opened your ClipBucketV5 Account, the date you last logged into your ClipBucketV5 Account, your age (if you choose to make it public), the country and the number of videos you have watched.</li>\r\n <li>Your ClipBucketV5 Account name, not your email address, is displayed to other users when you engage in certain activities on ClipBucketV5, such as when you upload videos or send  messages through ClipBucketV5. Other users can contact you by leaving a message or comment on the site.</li>\r\n <li>Any videos that you submit to ClipBucketV5 may be redistributed through the internet and other media channels, and may be viewed by other ClipBucketV5 users or the general public.</li>\r\n <li>You may also choose to add personal information which may include your name, gender, profile picture or other details, that will be visible to other users on your ClipBucketV5 Account channel page. If you choose to add certain features to your ClipBucketV5 Account channel page, then these features and your activity associated with these features will be displayed to other users and may be aggregated and shared with your friends or other users. Such shared activity may include your favorite videos, videos you rated and videos that you have uploaded.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>Your Choices</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>If you have a ClipBucketV5 Account, you may update or correct your personal profile information, email preferences and privacy settings at any time by visiting your account profile page.</li>\r\n  <li>You may control the information that is available to other users and your confirmed friends at any time by editing your ClipBucketV5 Account and the features that are included on your channel page. If you have enabled Active Sharing, other users may see that you, as identified by your account name, not your email address, are watching the same video.</li>\r\n <li>You may, of course, decline to submit personal information through ClipBucketV5, in which case you can still view videos and explore ClipBucketV5, but ClipBucketV5 may not be able to provide certain services to you.. The privacy notices of those services govern the use of your personal information associated with them.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n'),
(3, @language_id, 'Terms of Service', 'Write your own terms of service...'),
(4, @language_id, 'Help', '<span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">How to use ClipBucketV5</span><br><ol><li>Articles will be written pretty soon</li></ol>'),
(5, @language_id, 'How to activate AudioTrack API', '<div class="col-xs-12" lang="en"> <div class="page-header"> <h1 style="font-size: 36px;">How to activate AudioTrack API</p> <h3>Choose a video’s audio language</h1> <p class="lead">Some videos offer multiple audio tracks. To select them, your browser may need an additional setting.</p> <p>The <code>audioTracks</code> API allows the player to access the audio tracks recognized by the browser. Its availability depends on the browser, video format and playback mode.</p> <p class="small text-muted"><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLMediaElement/audioTracks">audioTracks API (MDN)</a></p> </div> <div class="alert alert-warning"> <p><strong>Before changing a setting</strong></p> <p>Experimental options in Chrome, Edge and Opera also enable other features, across all websites. They may cause problems. Note the original value so you can restore it. The website cannot enable these options for you.</p> </div> <h2>Instructions by browser</h2> <p>Read the section for the browser you use. Internal addresses must be copied into its address bar, then opened by pressing Enter or Go.</p> <div class="panel panel-default"> <div class="panel-heading"> <h2 class="panel-title">Google Chrome</h2> <p class="small text-muted">Desktop and Android · Experimental option</p> </div> <div class="panel-body"> <ol> <li>Copy this address into a new tab:<br><code>chrome://flags//*#enable-experimental-web-platform-features</code></li>*/ <li>Find <strong>Experimental Web Platform features</strong> and select <strong>Enabled</strong> (enabled).</li> <li>Save your work in other tabs, then use <strong>Relaunch</strong> to restart the browser.</li> <li>Return to the website, reload the video and try the player’s audio track menu, if available.</li> </ol> <p class="small text-muted">To undo: restore the original value, usually <strong>Default</strong>, then restart Chrome. This procedure does not apply to Chrome on iPhone or iPad.</p> <p class="small text-muted"><a href="https://developer.chrome.com/docs/web-platform/chrome-flags">Experimental options (Chrome)</a></p> </div> </div> <div class="panel panel-default"> <div class="panel-heading"> <h2 class="panel-title">Microsoft Edge</h2> <p class="small text-muted">Desktop · Experimental option</p> </div> <div class="panel-body"> <ol> <li>Open this address in Edge:<br><code>edge://flags//*#enable-experimental-web-platform-features</code></li>*/ <li>Set <strong>Experimental Web Platform features</strong> to <strong>Enabled</strong>.</li> <li>Save your work and click the restart button provided.</li> <li>Reload the video, then try switching the audio track in the player.</li> </ol> <p class="small text-muted">To undo: restore the original value, usually <strong>Default</strong>, then restart Edge. This option is not guaranteed to be available on mobile.</p> <p class="small text-muted"><a href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/blob/main/api/HTMLMediaElement.json">MDN compatibility data</a></p> </div> </div> <div class="panel panel-default"> <div class="panel-heading"> <h2 class="panel-title">Mozilla Firefox</h2> <p class="small text-muted">Desktop · Limited support</p> </div> <div class="panel-body"> <p><strong>Enabling the API is not enough to make multitrack playback work.</strong> Mozilla states that Firefox does not support multiple audio/video tracks in this context. This setting may expose the API without allowing you to choose another language.</p> <p>To enable access to the API only:</p> <ol> <li>Type <code>about:config</code> in the address bar.</li> <li>Read the warning and continue if you want to change this advanced setting.</li> <li>Search for <code>media.track.enabled</code>.</li> <li>If this preference exists, set its value to <strong>true</strong>, then reload the video. If it is missing, do not create it: doing so does not guarantee support.</li> </ol> <p class="small text-muted">To undo: restore the previous value. This guide does not provide a reliable procedure for Firefox on Android; access to advanced settings varies by edition.</p> <p class="small text-muted"><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Firefox/Experimental_features#htmlmediaelement_properties_audiotracks_and_videotracks">Firefox limitations (Mozilla)</a></p> </div> </div> <div class="panel panel-default"> <div class="panel-heading"> <h2 class="panel-title">Apple Safari</h2> <p class="small text-muted">Mac, iPhone and iPad · No activation required</p> </div> <div class="panel-body"> <p>Safari supports the <code>audioTracks</code> API without enabling experimental features.</p> <ol> <li>Open the video in Safari and start playback.</li> <li>Open the player’s audio track menu, if it appears, and choose your preferred language.</li> </ol> <p>If the menu is missing, check that the video has multiple usable tracks. Their availability also depends on the format and the player used by the website.</p> <p class="small text-muted"><a href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/blob/main/api/HTMLMediaElement.json">MDN compatibility data</a></p> </div> </div> <div class="panel panel-default"> <div class="panel-heading"> <h2 class="panel-title">Opera</h2> <p class="small text-muted">Desktop · Experimental option</p> </div> <div class="panel-body"> <ol> <li>Open this address in Opera:<br><code>opera://flags//*#enable-experimental-web-platform-features</code></li>*/ <li>If the <strong>Experimental Web Platform features</strong> option is available, select <strong>Enabled</strong>.</li> <li>Save your work, restart Opera using the button provided and reload the video.</li> </ol> <p class="small text-muted">To undo: restore the original value, usually <strong>Default</strong>, then restart Opera. Do not apply this procedure to Opera Mini or mobile editions without checking that the option is available.</p> <p class="small text-muted"><a href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/blob/main/api/HTMLMediaElement.json">MDN compatibility data</a></p> </div> </div> <div class="panel panel-default"> <div class="panel-heading"> <h2 class="panel-title">Brave</h2> <p class="small text-muted">Desktop · Experimental option</p> </div> <div class="panel-body"> <ol> <li>Open this address in Brave:<br><code>brave://flags//*#enable-experimental-web-platform-features</code></li>*/ <li>If the <strong>Experimental Web Platform features</strong> option is available, select <strong>Enabled</strong>.</li> <li>Save your work, restart Brave using the button provided and reload the video.</li> <li>Try the player’s audio track menu, if available.</li> </ol> <p>This procedure relies on experimental options inherited from Chromium. Their availability and multitrack functionality are not guaranteed in every version of Brave.</p> <p class="small text-muted">To undo: restore the original value, usually <strong>Default</strong>, then restart Brave. This procedure does not apply to Brave on iPhone or iPad.</p> <p class="small text-muted"><a href="https://github.com/chromium/chromium/blob/main/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/RuntimeEnabledFeatures.md">Chromium engine experimental options</a></p> </div> </div> <div class="panel panel-default"> <div class="panel-heading"> <h2 class="panel-title">Other browsers and mobile devices</h2> </div> <div class="panel-body"> <p><strong>iPhone and iPad:</strong> the desktop settings procedures for Chrome, Edge and Firefox do not apply as written. If you encounter a problem, open the same video in Safari, where the API is available without this setting.</p> <p><strong>Vivaldi, Samsung Internet and other browsers:</strong> a shared browser engine alone does not guarantee that the setting exists or works. If the API is missing and your browser offers no documented option, there is no universal way to enable it from the website.</p> </div> </div> <div class="well"> <h2>Still no other audio track?</h2> <ul> <li><strong>Restart, then reload:</strong> after changing an experimental setting, closing a single tab is not a substitute for restarting the browser.</li> <li><strong>Check the video:</strong> not all videos offer multiple languages. An accessible API does not add tracks to a file.</li> <li><strong>Cannot find the option:</strong> it may be missing from your version or blocked on a managed device. Do not change other options at random.</li> <li><strong>API accessible, but no menu:</strong> the format, codecs or the website’s playback mode may limit the available tracks. Tell support which video is affected, along with your browser, its version and your device.</li> </ul> <p>These settings concern audio track selection, not volume, subtitles or speaker selection.</p> </div> <hr> <div class="small text-muted"> <p>Documentation consulted on October 29, 2026. Browser options may change.</p> </div> </div>');
INSERT INTO `{tbl_prefix}pages_translations` (`page_id`, `language_id`, `page_title`, `page_content`) VALUES
(5, @language_id, 'Comment activer l''API AudioTrack', '<div class="col-xs-12" lang="fr"><div class="page-header"><h1 style="font-size: 36px;">Comment activer l''API AudioTrack</h1><h3>Choisir la langue audio d’une vidéo</h3><p class="lead">Certaines vidéos proposent plusieurs pistes audio. Pour les sélectionner, votre navigateur peut avoir besoin d’un réglage supplémentaire.</p><p>L’API <code>audioTracks</code> permet au lecteur d’accéder aux pistes audio reconnues par le navigateur. Sa disponibilité dépend du navigateur, du format de la vidéo et du mode de lecture.</p><p class="small text-muted"><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLMediaElement/audioTracks">API audioTracks (MDN)</a></p></div><div class="alert alert-warning"><p><strong>Avant de modifier un réglage</strong></p><p>Les options expérimentales de Chrome, Edge et Opera activent aussi d’autres fonctions, pour l’ensemble des sites. Elles peuvent provoquer des dysfonctionnements. Notez la valeur initiale pour pouvoir la restaurer. Le site ne peut pas activer ces options à votre place.</p></div><h2>Instructions par navigateur</h2><p>Consultez la rubrique correspondant au navigateur que vous utilisez. Les adresses internes doivent être copiées dans sa barre d’adresse, puis validées.</p><div class="panel panel-default"><div class="panel-heading"><h2 class="panel-title">Google Chrome</h2><p class="small text-muted">Ordinateur et Android · Option expérimentale</p></div><div class="panel-body"><ol><li>Copiez cette adresse dans un nouvel onglet :<br><code>chrome://flags/#enable-experimental-web-platform-features</code></li><li>Repérez <strong>Experimental Web Platform features</strong> et choisissez <strong>Enabled</strong> (activé).</li><li>Enregistrez votre travail dans les autres onglets, puis utilisez <strong>Relaunch</strong> pour relancer le navigateur.</li><li>Revenez sur le site, rechargez la vidéo et essayez le menu des pistes audio du lecteur, s’il est proposé.</li></ol><p class="small text-muted">Pour annuler : restaurez la valeur initiale, généralement <strong>Default</strong>, puis relancez Chrome. Cette procédure ne concerne pas Chrome sur iPhone ou iPad.</p><p class="small text-muted"><a href="https://developer.chrome.com/docs/web-platform/chrome-flags">Options expérimentales (Chrome)</a></p></div></div><div class="panel panel-default"><div class="panel-heading"><h2 class="panel-title">Microsoft Edge</h2><p class="small text-muted">Ordinateur · Option expérimentale</p></div><div class="panel-body"><ol><li>Ouvrez cette adresse dans Edge :<br><code>edge://flags/#enable-experimental-web-platform-features</code></li><li>Réglez <strong>Experimental Web Platform features</strong> sur <strong>Enabled</strong>.</li><li>Enregistrez votre travail et cliquez sur le bouton de redémarrage proposé.</li><li>Rechargez la vidéo, puis essayez de changer la piste audio dans le lecteur.</li></ol><p class="small text-muted">Pour annuler : restaurez la valeur initiale, généralement <strong>Default</strong>, puis redémarrez Edge. La disponibilité de cette option sur mobile n’est pas garantie.</p><p class="small text-muted"><a href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/blob/main/api/HTMLMediaElement.json">Données de compatibilité MDN</a></p></div></div><div class="panel panel-default"><div class="panel-heading"><h2 class="panel-title">Mozilla Firefox</h2><p class="small text-muted">Ordinateur · Prise en charge limitée</p></div><div class="panel-body"><p><strong>Activer l’API ne suffit pas à rendre la lecture multipiste opérationnelle.</strong> Mozilla indique que Firefox ne prend pas en charge plusieurs pistes audio/vidéo dans ce cadre. Ce réglage peut exposer l’API sans permettre de choisir une autre langue.</p><p>Pour activer uniquement l’accès à l’API :</p><ol><li>Saisissez <code>about:config</code> dans la barre d’adresse.</li><li>Lisez l’avertissement et continuez si vous souhaitez modifier ce réglage avancé.</li><li>Recherchez <code>media.track.enabled</code>.</li><li>Si cette préférence existe, passez sa valeur à <strong>true</strong>, puis rechargez la vidéo. Si elle est absente, ne la créez pas : cela ne garantit pas la prise en charge.</li></ol><p class="small text-muted">Pour annuler : restaurez la valeur précédente. Ce guide ne propose pas de procédure fiable pour Firefox sur Android ; l’accès aux réglages avancés varie selon l’édition.</p><p class="small text-muted"><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Firefox/Experimental_features#htmlmediaelement_properties_audiotracks_and_videotracks">Limites de Firefox (Mozilla)</a></p></div></div><div class="panel panel-default"><div class="panel-heading"><h2 class="panel-title">Apple Safari</h2><p class="small text-muted">Mac, iPhone et iPad · Pas d’activation requise</p></div><div class="panel-body"><p>Safari prend en charge l’API <code>audioTracks</code> sans activation expérimentale.</p><ol><li>Ouvrez la vidéo dans Safari et lancez sa lecture.</li><li>Ouvrez le menu des pistes audio du lecteur, s’il apparaît, et choisissez la langue souhaitée.</li></ol><p>Si le menu est absent, vérifiez que la vidéo possède plusieurs pistes utilisables. Leur disponibilité dépend aussi du format et du lecteur utilisé par le site.</p><p class="small text-muted"><a href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/blob/main/api/HTMLMediaElement.json">Données de compatibilité MDN</a></p></div></div><div class="panel panel-default"><div class="panel-heading"><h2 class="panel-title">Opera</h2><p class="small text-muted">Ordinateur · Option expérimentale</p></div><div class="panel-body"><ol><li>Ouvrez cette adresse dans Opera :<br><code>opera://flags/#enable-experimental-web-platform-features</code></li><li>Si l’option <strong>Experimental Web Platform features</strong> est disponible, choisissez <strong>Enabled</strong>.</li><li>Enregistrez votre travail, relancez Opera avec le bouton proposé et rechargez la vidéo.</li></ol><p class="small text-muted">Pour annuler : restaurez la valeur initiale, généralement <strong>Default</strong>, puis relancez Opera. Ne transposez pas cette procédure à Opera Mini ou aux éditions mobiles sans vérifier la présence de l’option.</p><p class="small text-muted"><a href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/blob/main/api/HTMLMediaElement.json">Données de compatibilité MDN</a></p></div></div><div class="panel panel-default"><div class="panel-heading"><h2 class="panel-title">Brave</h2><p class="small text-muted">Ordinateur · Option expérimentale</p></div><div class="panel-body"><ol><li>Ouvrez cette adresse dans Brave :<br><code>brave://flags/#enable-experimental-web-platform-features</code></li><li>Si l’option <strong>Experimental Web Platform features</strong> est disponible, choisissez <strong>Enabled</strong>.</li><li>Enregistrez votre travail, relancez Brave avec le bouton proposé et rechargez la vidéo.</li><li>Essayez le menu des pistes audio du lecteur, s’il est proposé.</li></ol><p>Cette procédure repose sur les options expérimentales héritées de Chromium. Leur disponibilité et le fonctionnement du multipiste ne sont pas garantis dans toutes les versions de Brave.</p><p class="small text-muted">Pour annuler : restaurez la valeur initiale, généralement <strong>Default</strong>, puis relancez Brave. Cette procédure ne concerne pas Brave sur iPhone ou iPad.</p><p class="small text-muted"><a href="https://github.com/chromium/chromium/blob/main/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/RuntimeEnabledFeatures.md">Options expérimentales du moteur Chromium</a></p></div></div><div class="panel panel-default"><div class="panel-heading"><h2 class="panel-title">Autres navigateurs et appareils mobiles</h2></div><div class="panel-body"><p><strong>iPhone et iPad :</strong> les procédures de réglage pour Chrome, Edge et Firefox sur ordinateur ne s’appliquent pas telles quelles. Si vous rencontrez un problème, ouvrez la même vidéo dans Safari, où l’API est disponible sans ce réglage.</p><p><strong>Vivaldi, Samsung Internet et autres navigateurs :</strong> leur moteur commun éventuel ne suffit pas à garantir la présence du réglage ou son fonctionnement. Si l’API est absente et qu’aucune option documentée n’est proposée par votre navigateur, il n’existe pas d’activation universelle depuis le site.</p></div></div><div class="well"><h2>Toujours aucune autre piste audio ?</h2><ul><li><strong>Relancez puis rechargez :</strong> après une modification expérimentale, fermer un seul onglet ne remplace pas le redémarrage du navigateur.</li><li><strong>Vérifiez la vidéo :</strong> toutes les vidéos ne proposent pas plusieurs langues. Une API accessible n’ajoute pas de piste à un fichier.</li><li><strong>Option introuvable :</strong> elle peut être absente de votre version ou bloquée sur un appareil administré. Ne modifiez pas d’autres options au hasard.</li><li><strong>API accessible, mais menu absent :</strong> le format, les codecs ou le mode de lecture du site peuvent limiter les pistes disponibles. Signalez au support la vidéo concernée, votre navigateur, sa version et votre appareil.</li></ul><p>Ces réglages concernent la sélection d’une piste audio, pas le volume, les sous-titres ou le choix des haut-parleurs.</p></div><hr><div class="small text-muted"><p>Documentation consultée le 29 octobre 2026. Les options des navigateurs peuvent évoluer.</p></div></div>');